*** Although this example is not completed (GNutella protocol is not written), it 
is functional and runnable (working like echo), so one can implement gnutella protocol 
here :-) ***

It is supposed to show on GNutella protocol example how to use multithreaded server classes
for building lightweight JDK1.0 compliant P2P client (light multithreaded server -- without Thread
pool has been used for accepting connections) using the framework on the lower 
layer than Messages (direct access to Input/Output streams).


For running the example:

1.cd to the example directory;
2.start runServer.sh under Unix or runServer.bat under Win
3.start runClient.sh under Unix or runClient.bat under Win

